    "f_anchor_tier_1_candidate": "The Scholz ratio E[3^r_3 imag] / E[3^r_3 real] = 3/2 is a direct theorem-level consequence of Scholz reflection 1932 + CL distributional asymptotics. Tier-1 anchor candidate: any future LMFDB update should preserve this ratio converging to 1.5 at |disc| \u2192 \u221e. Currently 1.489 at bucket 6 (|disc| ~ 10^6, n=381K); projection to |disc| ~ 10^8 predicts ratio ~1.498.",
    "connection_to_r18e_dh_anchor": "R18e confirmed \u03b1_{p=3} = 1/6 (Davenport-Heilbronn) at 0.1\u03c3 imag, 0.67\u03c3 real. R18f confirms the Scholz ratio 3/2 at 1% level. These are the same 3-torsion structure viewed from different angles \u2014 the rate of convergence (\u03b1 = 1/6) and the limiting moment ratio (3/2). Both anchors are proved theorems matching empirical at LMFDB-scale.",
    "remaining_frontier": "The ~1% residual from 1.5 at bucket 6 is NOT a frontier signal \u2014 it matches BST finite-|disc| bias. But the RATE at which the Scholz ratio converges (currently ~1/decade of |disc|) could itself be fit and compared to DH 1/6. Leaving for future work."
